<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>AI Summer Camp - Task 2: Feature Extraction</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/task2.css">
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@300;400;600;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/6.4.0/css/all.min.css">
</head>
<body>
    <div class="container">
        <div class="task-card">
            <!-- Header Section -->
            <div class="header-section">
                <a href="/lobby" class="back-btn">
                    <i class="fas fa-arrow-left"></i>
                    Back to Lobby
                </a>
                <a href="/logout" class="logout-btn">
                    <i class="fas fa-sign-out-alt"></i>
                    Logout
                </a>
            </div>

            <div class="task-header">
                <h1 class="task-title">Step 2: Manual Feature Extraction Challenge</h1>
                <p class="task-subtitle">Learning how AI scientists identify key characteristics to classify objects</p>
            </div>

            <!-- Introduction Section -->
            <div class="intro-section">
                <h2 class="section-title">Before Modern AI: Manual Feature Extraction</h2>
                <div class="intro-content">
                    <div class="generic-pyramid">
                        <img src="/images/Task 2/generic.JPG" alt="Generic Pyramid" class="generic-img">
                    </div>
                    <div class="intro-text">
                        <p class="description-text">
                            Before developing proper automatic feature extraction mechanisms, AI scientists had to 
                            study the data and manually extract differentiators in order to properly classify objects. 
                            This process required <span class="highlight">data scientists</span> to identify the most 
                            important characteristics that distinguish one type of object from another.
                        </p>
                        <p class="description-text">
                            In this task, you'll learn how this manual feature extraction works by identifying 
                            key differences between Egyptian and Mayan pyramids.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Training Data Section -->
            <div class="training-section">
                <h2 class="section-title">Training Examples</h2>
                <p class="section-subtitle">Study these examples to understand the key differences</p>
                <div class="training-grid">
                    <div class="training-item egyptian">
                        <h3 class="item-title">Egyptian Pyramids</h3>
                        <div class="mushroom-image">
                            <img src="/images/Task 2/egyptian 1.jpg" alt="Egyptian Pyramid Example" class="training-img">
                        </div>
                        <div class="features-list">
                            <h4 class="features-title">Key Features:</h4>
                            <ul class="features">
                                <li><strong>Shape:</strong> Smooth, sloping sides that come to a point at the top.</li>
                                <li><strong>Purpose:</strong> Built as tombs for pharaohs to ascend to the afterlife.</li>
                                <li><strong>Construction:</strong> Large, precisely cut limestone blocks with minimal mortar.</li>
                                <li><strong>Top Structure:</strong> Sharp pointed apex with no additional platforms.</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="training-item mayan">
                        <h3 class="item-title">Mayan Pyramids</h3>
                        <div class="mushroom-image">
                            <img src="/images/Task 2/mayan 1.jpg" alt="Mayan Pyramid Example" class="training-img">
                        </div>
                        <div class="features-list">
                            <h4 class="features-title">Key Features:</h4>
                            <ul class="features">
                                <li><strong>Shape:</strong> Stepped, terraced structures with distinct levels and edges.</li>
                                <li><strong>Purpose:</strong> Built as temples and ceremonial centers for rituals.</li>
                                <li><strong>Construction:</strong> Smaller stone blocks, rubble, and mortar construction.</li>
                                <li><strong>Top Structure:</strong> Flat top platform often with temple buildings.</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Testing Section -->
            <div class="testing-section">
                <h2 class="section-title">Step 2: Classify These New Pyramids</h2>
                <p class="section-subtitle">Look at the new pictures below. Based on what you observed, are they "Egyptian" or "Mayan" pyramids?</p>
                
                <div class="testing-grid">
                    <div class="test-item">
                        <div class="mushroom-image">
                            <img src="/images/Task 2/egyptian 2.jpg" alt="Pyramid A" class="test-img">
                        </div>
                        <label for="answer1" class="test-label">Pyramid A</label>
                        <div class="features-list">
                            <p class="observed-features"><strong>Observed Features:</strong></p>
                            <ul class="feature-tags">
                                <li>Shape: Smooth</li>
                                <li>Purpose: Tomb</li>
                                <li>Construction: Large blocks</li>
                                <li>Top: Pointed</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                        <select id="answer1" class="answer-select">
                            <option value="">Choose classification...</option>
                            <option value="Egyptian">Egyptian Pyramid</option>
                            <option value="Mayan">Mayan Pyramid</option>
                        </select>
                    </div>
                    <div class="test-item">
                        <div class="mushroom-image">
                            <img src="/images/Task 2/mayan 2.jpg" alt="Pyramid B" class="test-img">
                        </div>
                        <label for="answer2" class="test-label">Pyramid B</label>
                        <div class="features-list">
                            <p class="observed-features"><strong>Observed Features:</strong></p>
                            <ul class="feature-tags">
                                <li>Shape: Stepped</li>
                                <li>Purpose: Temple</li>
                                <li>Construction: Small blocks</li>
                                <li>Top: Flat platform</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                        <select id="answer2" class="answer-select">
                            <option value="">Choose classification...</option>
                            <option value="Egyptian">Egyptian Pyramid</option>
                            <option value="Mayan">Mayan Pyramid</option>
                        </select>
                    </div>
                </div>
                
                <div class="unclear-section">
                    <p class="unclear-explanation">
                        This process is amazing in images where distinguishing patterns are unclear. 
                        Even when visual details are hard to see, the extracted features help us make informed classifications:
                    </p>
                    
                    <div class="test-item unclear-item">
                        <div class="mushroom-image">
                            <img src="/images/Task 2/unclear.png" alt="Pyramid C" class="test-img">
                        </div>
                        <label for="answer3" class="test-label">Pyramid C</label>
                        <div class="features-list">
                            <p class="observed-features"><strong>Observed Features:</strong></p>
                            <ul class="feature-tags">
                                <li>Shape: Stepped and Smooth</li>
                                <li>Purpose: Tomb</li>
                                <li>Construction: Large blocks</li>
                                <li>Top: Flat</li>
                                <li>Location: Middle East</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                        <select id="answer3" class="answer-select">
                            <option value="">Choose classification...</option>
                            <option value="Egyptian">Egyptian Pyramid</option>
                            <option value="Mayan">Mayan Pyramid</option>
                        </select>
                    </div>
                </div>
                
                <div class="submit-section">
                    <button id="checkButton" class="submit-btn">
                        <span>Check My Answers</span>
                        <div class="btn-icon">
                            <i class="fas fa-check"></i>
                        </div>
                    </button>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Feedback Section -->
            <div id="feedback" class="feedback-section hidden">
                <h3 class="feedback-title">Your Results</h3>
                <div id="score-display" class="score-display"></div>
                <ul id="feedback-list" class="feedback-list"></ul>
                
                <!-- Educational Explanation -->
                <div id="explanation" class="explanation-section">
                    <h4 class="explanation-title">What Just Happened?</h4>
                     <p class="explanation-text">
                        You just performed manual feature extraction! You observed patterns like shape (smooth vs. stepped), construction style, and top structure 
                        to make your classifications.
                    </p>

                    <p class="explanation-text">
                        What you just did is exactly how early <strong>machine learning</strong> worked! <strong>Data scientists</strong> 
                        would manually study datasets and identify the most important features that distinguish between 
                        different categories. They would then extract these features and use them to train classification models.
                    </p>

                    <p class="explanation-text">
                        Modern AI has automated much of this feature extraction process through <strong>deep learning</strong>, 
                        but understanding manual feature engineering helps us appreciate how AI learns to identify patterns 
                        and make decisions based on data characteristics.
                    </p>
                </div>
                
                <div class="next-section">
                    <button id="nextButton" class="next-btn">
                        <span>Continue to Next Task</span>
                        <div class="btn-icon">
                            <i class="fas fa-arrow-right"></i>
                        </div>
                    </button>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <script src="/js/task2.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
